I added a `unit` project to `vitest.config.ts` that runs `test/unit/**/*.test.ts`. The `integration` project is unchanged.

```ts
{
  // Don't inherit the root options, so the database setup file doesn't run.
  extends: false,
  test: {
    name: "unit",
    include: ["test/unit/**/*.test.ts"],
  },
},
```

I haven't run it. The commands to run the tests needed permission and weren't approved, so it's untested. To check it, run `npx vitest run --project unit`: it should pass quickly without starting Docker.

The unit project sets `extends: false`, so it doesn't inherit the root `setupFiles` and never loads `test/setup-db.ts`. (In vitest 5, inline projects inherit the root options unless you turn that off.)
